<figure class="cache-figure" data-sentinel-quorum>
 <p class="figure-title">Detecting failure and authorising promotion are separate decisions</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>Configured Sentinels <select data-total aria-label="Configured Sentinels"><option value="3">3</option><option value="5" selected>5</option></select></label><label>Connected group <input data-reachable type="range" min="1" max="5" value="2" /></label><label><input data-eligible type="checkbox" checked /> An eligible replica is reachable</label></div>
 <div class="sentinel-partitions"><div><b>This connected group</b><div class="sentinel-nodes" data-connected></div><small>All report the primary down</small></div><div><b>Other Sentinels</b><div class="sentinel-nodes" data-isolated></div><small>Cannot vote with this group</small></div></div>
 <div class="sentinel-gates"><p data-detect></p><p data-authorise></p><p data-promote></p></div>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>Quorum is fixed at 2. Every Sentinel in the connected group can communicate with its peers and reports the primary down; the others are isolated from it. This model tests necessary vote counts and replica availability, not detection timers, elections, competing views or actual failover duration. A real deployment must also satisfy replica-selection and reachability rules.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import{sentinelDecision}from'../../lib/caching/recovery.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-sentinel-quorum]').forEach(root=>{const total=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-total]')!,reachable=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-reachable]')!,eligible=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-eligible]')!;const render=()=>{const n=Number(total.value);reachable.max=String(n);if(Number(reachable.value)>n)reachable.value=String(n);const k=Number(reachable.value),s=sentinelDecision(n,k,eligible.checked);reachable.setAttribute('aria-valuetext',`${k} of ${n} Sentinels`);for(const[target,begin,end]of[['connected',1,k],['isolated',k+1,n]] as const){const group=root.querySelector(`[data-${target}]`)!;group.replaceChildren(...Array.from({length:end-begin+1},(_,i)=>{const el=document.createElement('span');el.textContent=`S${begin+i}`;return el;}));if(begin>end)group.textContent='None';}const lines=[['detect',s.detected,`Failure quorum: ${k} reports / ${s.quorum} needed`],['authorise',s.authorised,`Authorisation: ${k} votes / ${s.majority} needed`],['promote',eligible.checked,eligible.checked?'Eligible replica: reachable':'Eligible replica: unavailable']] as const;for(const[key,pass,label]of lines){const el=root.querySelector(`[data-${key}]`)!;el.textContent=`${pass?'✓':'—'} ${label}`;el.classList.toggle('passed',pass);}root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=!s.detected?'This group cannot even reach the configured failure quorum.':!s.authorised?'Two reports establish the failure quorum, but this group has no majority. It cannot authorise a failover.':!eligible.checked?'The vote counts are sufficient, but votes cannot create an eligible replica. No promotion is available.':'The group has sufficient reports, a majority and a reachable eligible replica. These conditions permit a failover attempt; they do not prove every acknowledged write will survive.';};total.onchange=render;reachable.oninput=render;eligible.onchange=render;render();});
</script>
